    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • 2026 Paris Motor Show: Jeep Reveals Six-Model European Strategy for 2030, Renegade Is Set to Return\nFord Rolls Out 2027 Mustang Mach-E Trail Package\n19 photos\nPhoto: Ford\nTrail and Mustang in the same model name seems nonsensical, but the same could be said about the Rally version of the Mach-E. For model year 2027, the Ford Motor Company has borrowed a few bits from the Rally grade for the all-new Trail package. Said option adds $2,295 to the final price of the Select eAWD.\nBeyond this change, Ford has opened the order banks for the 2027 Mustang Mach-E line. Across the board, the extended-range battery is now standard. This, in turn, pushes the entry price to $39,995 as opposed to $37,795 for the 2026 model.\nHaving cleared that up, what's in the package? Specially tuned passive struts and springs open the list, with said components lifting the front and rear axles 10 and 15 millimeters compared to the Select and Premium grades. That would be 0.4 and 0.6 inches in American English, which is not quite sufficient for the Mustang Mach-E Select eAWD Trail to be considered a true all-road machine.\nIts 19-inch High Gloss Dark Carbonized Gray as-cast graphics wheels and Michelin CrossClimate 2 rubber are shared with the Mustang Mach-E Rally, ensuring proper control and grip across a wide variety of surfaces and conditions. Also shared with the Rally is the steering rack.\nThe Carbon Black lower fascia and Trail logo on the center armrest bring the point home. As for the reason why the Ford Motor Company decided to develop this package, bear in mind the Rally is a lot pricier. With the Trail, the Dearborn-based automaker hopes to attract customers that would have otherwise looked elsewhere due to the Rally's exorbitant starting price.\nPhoto: Ford Trail goodies further include standard 400-watt Pro Power Onboard, which is kind of curious because it's an optional extra on the Premium, GT, and Rally. When it comes to Trail options, Ford calls attention to a couple of things. First and foremost, the Interior Protection Package brings a cargo area protector and all-weather floor mats.\nThe Clamp On Cross Bar Kit by Thule is the niche option, carrying gear boxes, bicycles, and kayaks on top of the vehicle. That being said, most versions of the 2027 Mustang Mach-E for the US market ship with an 88-kWh battery. The GT and Rally level up to 91 kilowatt-hours.\n$2,200 more expensive than before for its least exciting of specifications, the Mustang Mach-E drops the old secondary drive unit for a new design. While this front-mounted electric motor may deliver the same performance, Ford claims it does so at a lower cost. BlueCruise 1.5 is an extra on lesser grades, while GT and Rally get the suite by default.\nRegardless of grade, BlueCruise 1.5 comes with one year plus 90 days of service included. Both the Connectivity and Security packages go standard, with a year of service included. Shadow Black and Desert Sand are the only no-extra-cost paint colors, while extra-cost options include Velocity Blue Metallic, Race Red, Star White Metallic Tri-coat, Eruption Green Metallic , Adriatic Blue Metallic, and Glacier Gray Metallic.\nFoMoCo expects Trail shipments to kick off in the first quarter of 2027. Unfortunately, EPA driving range estimates will be announced later.\nVia // Ford\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nFord Mustang Mach-E Trail 2027 Ford Mustang Mach-E Trail 2027 Ford Mustang Mach-E Ford Mustang Mach-E Ford price specifications\nAbout the author: Mircea Panait\nAfter a 1:43 scale model of a Ferrari 250 GTO sparked Mircea's interest for cars when he was a kid, an early internship at Top Gear sealed his career path. He's most interested in muscle cars and American trucks, but he takes a passing interest in quirky kei cars as well. Full profile\nUP NEXT Himiway Took a Crack at Building an SUV E-Bike and Succeeded for Just $2,000 – Real Riders Approve",
